Backend (inference.py):
- Add CircadianNormalizer: inverted-U diurnal model (Monk et al. 1983), factor 0.70–1.15
  applied to raw load so high-capacity hours compress effective load; trough hours amplify it
- Add FlowEpisodeDetector: hysteresis FSM (entry < 0.32, exit > 0.42, min 8 windows)
  tracks discrete flow episodes with avg_depth, min_load, duration_ms, recovery_load
- CognitiveLoadEstimate gains circadian_factor, in_flow_episode, flow_episode_depth fields

Backend (analytics.py):
- Add GET /sessions/{id}/segments: chronological cognitive segment map (flow/overload/normal
  episodes) replayed from session load stream; returns flow_time_fraction and per-segment stats
- Add GET /sessions/{id}/correlations: Pearson r between each behavioural signal and load score,
  ranked by |r|; top_signal field identifies the dominant load driver for the session

SDK (NeuroFlow.ts):
- Add CSSInterpolator: rAF-based exponential lerp for all --nf-load-derived CSS vars;
  eliminates step-change jumps between server estimates at ~60fps
- Add applySensitivityZones: per-element --nf-load override via data-nf-sensitivity multiplier
- Add focus tunnel: in minimal state, non-focused elements get data-nf-defocused attribute
- Add classifyMode: infers "reading" | "writing" | "idle" from dominant signal; sets data-nf-mode
- New CSS vars: --nf-circadian, --nf-flow-depth; new attributes: data-nf-flow, data-nf-mode

Extension (collector.js):
- Add per-domain calibration via chrome.storage.local; factor persisted across sessions,
  updated with 70/30 blend at session end; sent with every signal as domain_calibration
- Add cognitive recovery rate signal: tracks load slope in RECOVERY_WINDOW post-peak windows,
  normalised to [0,1], exponentially smoothed; sent as recovery_rate

Extension (background.js):
- Push LOAD_ESTIMATE messages back to content scripts for calibration/recovery tracking
- Add flow episode badge flash (⚡) when in_flow_episode is true

Reference app (AdaptiveEditor.tsx):
- Add adaptive syntax highlighting: full colour palette in rich/normal; pruned to
  keywords+strings in reduced; near-monochrome in minimal (HighlightStyle per state)
- Add progressive comment auto-fold: foldAll() on transition into high-load states,
  unfoldAll() on recovery; uses CodeMirror foldAll/unfoldAll from @codemirror/language
- Add tooltip verbosity control: data-nf-tooltip-verbosity attribute ("full"/"brief"/"none")
  on editor wrapper for companion CSS to control hover doc length

